I had never tasted Greek food until I stopped at the Greek Lady. This restaurant used to be operated out of a food cart, but it was so popular that the owner decided to operate out of a restaurant.

Though I recommend their gyros, their "American" food is amazing as well. The salads are HUGE and are enough for 2 meals. I love the fries and the chicken finger hoagie. You have never tasted pita bread until you have had some from here. My mouth waters just thinking about this soft and chewy bread.

Because of its popularity, expect a wait around lunch time. During the school year, the Greek Lady stays busy through out the night. Good thing they have delivery! &#61514;

still amazing!
the pig and miso ramen is my fave bc its closest to the "traditional" ramen with pork based tonkotsu flavor plus miso. 

if you have the chance to go for lunch, they have a great special - instead of $10-12 for a bowl of ramen, for $13 you get a house salad, an appetizer like fried chicken or gyoza (dumplings), and a bowl of ramen! got it today, it was great :)

Driving all the way from New York, this place had been recommended by many of my friends.. To my surprise it was absolutely nothing like it was described. I was beyond disappointed being that I had driven a total of 3 and a half hours just to try these amazing "cheesesteaks" everyone always tells me about. Friday July 20th in the afternoon, I finally get in line to order and had to have been helped by the most disgusting person I've dealt with anywhere yet. And being that I'm from New York, I deal with a bunch of A******* on a daily already. As soon as I was about to finish placing my order I asked if I can PLEASE have extra cheese. And BEFORE my cheesesteak was even wrapped AND before they had started making my second order she said..RUDELY, "Well this one is already made." That response pissed me off, but whatever, in the moment I was hungry. Second cheesesteak was made, paid, sat, and started eating. I wasn't even given the right order. So after all that shitty service my order was messed up. And the way these were made, I most definitely did NOT get my money's worth. 

So after my shitty experience I walked across the street to GENO's and had a REAL Philly cheesesteak. I was finally content and very well satisfied I had finally gotten what I've been wanting to try now for over a year. So thank you GENO's. 

@yelp you should have an option for No Stars because that's how shitty that experience at Pat's was. They're definitely not the king of steaks.

Philadelphia airport covers the gamut from unhealthy to not-totally-unhealthy fast food establishments. From Chick-fil-A, to chickie and Pete's; Wendy's to McDonald's; and Curito Burrito to Earl of Sandwich and that sushi place;  

That said Popeyes is an underrated option if you're banished to the ends of C-terminal (I'm sorry, you're definitely flying USAir...). Really one of the better Popeye's I've been to. The service isn't super fast, and they don't have all the culinary options always covered on the hot bar, but what they do have tastes as good (or better) as any Popeyes I've been to... And I've been to a few. 

They'll also cook/fry you up anything on the menu if you're willing to wait a few minutes.

The fried oyster mushroom is very plain;
The fried chicken has detached skin and meat;
The fried squid is adequate, but it has a lot of fried shrimp chips underneath.

总得来说不值得再来，比我在台湾吃的赤炸差远了。
PS：碳烤系列还没上线...
